{
  "question": "Do resonator measurements in the laboratory and observation stations exhibit a genuine 3‑day lagged correlation beyond what random variation would predict?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "Shared environmental influence causing a 3‑day lag correlation",
      "probability": 0.30,
      "rationale": "The cross‑check between resonator_lab and resonator_obs shows a positive agreement of 0.398 at a 3‑day offset (n=42). If a common environmental factor (e.g., temperature, magnetic field) affects both instruments with a delayed response, this could produce the observed correlation.",
      "evidenceFor": ["crosscheck_reslab_resobs"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["chance_level"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Statistical fluctuation within random noise",
      "probability": 0.55,
      "rationale": "The observed agreement (0.398) does not exceed the chance threshold for the best offset (±0.447). Given the limited sample size, such a correlation can arise from random variation alone.",
      "evidenceFor": ["chance_level"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["crosscheck_reslab_resobs"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Systematic artifact in data acquisition or processing",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "Both resonator datasets were collected on the same calendar day using the same timing infrastructure. A shared timing error or processing pipeline could induce spurious lagged similarity.",
      "evidenceFor": ["event_1036534","event_789124","event_310753","event_91008"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.05,
  "summaryOfChange": "Previously the belief state was a single residual (1.00) with no defined question. Based on the new cross‑check showing a 0.398 agreement at a 3‑day offset, I formulated a specific question about a lagged resonator correlation and introduced three concrete hypotheses: a genuine shared influence (30%), pure statistical noise (55%), and a systematic artifact (10%). The remaining 5% is allocated to unknown factors. Probabilities were assigned de novo rather than tweaked from a prior distribution, reflecting the absence of earlier structured beliefs."
}

