{
  "question": "Why did the pendulum_lab instrument record a cluster of unusually high beat values on day 16 (trials 115‑120), deviating from its established baseline and post‑baseline drift?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "Random statistical fluctuation",
      "probability": 0.40,
      "rationale": "Even in a stable instrument, occasional runs of higher readings can occur by chance. The observed cluster could be an unlikely but still possible tail of the normal variation.",
      "evidenceFor": ["761412", "508173", "376706", "480762"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["508173", "376706", "480762"]
    },
    {
      "label": "Unrecognized systematic error in data acquisition",
      "probability": 0.35,
      "rationale": "A timing glitch, sensor mis‑calibration, or software bug affecting a block of consecutive measurements could produce a short‑term bias without altering longer‑term drift statistics.",
      "evidenceFor": ["761412", "508173", "376706", "480762", "119", "120"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    },
    {
      "label": "Transient local environmental perturbation",
      "probability": 0.20,
      "rationale": "A brief change in temperature, vibration, or magnetic field at the laboratory on day 16 could have altered the pendulum period, producing a temporary shift that does not persist into later days.",
      "evidenceFor": ["761412", "508173", "376706", "480762"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    },
    {
      "label": "Unmodeled physical phenomenon affecting pendulum period",
      "probability": 0.05,
      "rationale": "An as‑yet‑unknown physical effect (e.g., subtle mass redistribution in the settlement) could have temporarily altered the pendulum's dynamics. This remains highly speculative given the limited data.",
      "evidenceFor": ["761412", "508173", "376706", "480762"],
      "evidenceAgainst": []
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.0,
  "summaryOfChange": "Previously the focal question concerned a possible 3‑day lagged correlation between resonator_lab and resonator_obs measurements. New data from day 16 reveal an unexpected cluster of high pendulum_lab readings (events 761412‑480762) that were not addressed by the earlier hypotheses. Consequently I have replaced the prior question with one centered on this pendulum anomaly and rebuilt the hypothesis set to explain the observed deviation, reallocating probabilities from the earlier lag‑correlation scenario to these four explanations."
}

